            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <VentilationSystem>The House is quite air tight as the blower door test shows 1.71 Air Exchanges/hour. Currently the house is provided with supply air via the furnace and exhaust via bathroom and range hood fans.



There would be quite a few benefits of having a HRV/ERV installed.  It will improve air quality in the home as it will exhaust stale air and supply fresh heated air to the home. Also there is less of a chance you have to worry about a carbon monoxide leak if anything ever happened to your heating system, as the HRV would exhaust these fumes.



The HRV/ERV will recover heated exhaust air via a heat exchanger and preheat supply air with the extracted heat, making the units very efficient. Make sure the unit is ENERGY STARÂ® rated and HVI certified.



HRV = Heat Recovery Ventilator

ERV = Enthalpy Recovery Ventilator



ERV also can control indoor humidity levels as well.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on ventilation systems and the criteria for these products.

</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
